<title>USA: Samsonite stake cut by Cooperman group.</title>
<headline>Samsonite stake cut by Cooperman group.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-03-31</dateline>
<text>
<p>A group led bgy New York investor Leon Cooperman said Monday it cut its stake in Samsonite Corp to 1,028,412 common shares of 5.1 percent.</p>
<p>The group said its latest transactions included a net 45,200 common shares sold between February 7 and March 27 at prices ranging from $48 to $50.02 per share, In a filing with the Securities and Exchange Commission.</p>
<p>The luggage company is based in Denver.</p>
